  m_Name: Ending_OtherPanda
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Ending
  endingTitle: Panda
  titleDA: 'Sammen Med Den Anden Panda '
  descriptionDA: "Pandaerne deler omr\xE5det. Bambussen er knap, og de holder sandsynligvis
    ikke sammen l\xE6nge endnu, Men mens de er sammen, har de en chance for at f\xE5
    unger. \n\n   \nPandaer lever for det meste alene og m\xF8des kun kort om for\xE5ret
    for at parre sig. N\xE5r skoven bliver delt op, kan dyrene ikke n\xE5 hinanden,
    og bestanden bliver mere ensartet og mere s\xE5rbar. Sammenh\xE6ngende skov g\xF8r
    en forskel.\n\nN\xE5r du g\xE5r i zoo st\xF8tter du pandaerne, de er med i et
    avls program af China Wildlife Conservation Association som er del i at sikre
    pandaens langsigtede overlevelse. Hvis du skal k\xF8be bambus produkter kan du
    selv kigge efter FSC-m\xE6rkede produkter som garantere at vigtige levesteder
    ikke er blevet \xF8delagt. "
  titleEN: Together With The Other Panda
  descriptionEN: 'The pandas are sharing the area. The bamboo is limited, and they
    will likely not stay together for long, but while they are together, they have
    a chance to get cubs.


    Pandas usually live alone and only meet for a short
    period in spring to mate. When the forest is split up, the animals cannot reach
    each other, and the population becomes more uniform and more vulnerable. Connected
    forest makes a difference.


    When you go to the zoo you are supporting the
    pandas, as they are a part of a breeding program for CHina Wildlife Conservation
    Association which ensures the pandas longterm survival. If you have to buy bamboo
    products, then you can look for FSC-labled products which gaurentee that important
    habitats do not get destroyed.'
  endingImage: {fileID: 0}
  endingDescription: dadadad
